<p>The Africa Centres for Disease Control and Prevention confirmed a new Ebola outbreak Friday in the Democratic Republic of the Congo’s northeastern Ituri province, reporting 246 suspected cases and 65 deaths. Most suspected cases and deaths were in the Mongwalu and Rwampara health zones; suspected cases were also reported in Bunia, Ituri’s provincial capital, pending confirmation. Africa CDC said preliminary laboratory tests detected Ebola virus in 13 of 20 samples, with four deaths among laboratory-confirmed cases. Initial findings pointed to a non-Zaire strain of Ebola, and sequencing was still underway to characterize the virus. Africa CDC said it was convening an urgent coordination meeting with Congo, Uganda, South Sudan and global partners on cross-border surveillance, preparedness and response. Uganda later reported an imported Ebola case in which a patient died in Kampala, according to DW and Ars Technica. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus said the organization had sent a team last week to help Congo investigate and collect samples, and WHO allocated $500,000 from its emergency fund for surveillance and response work.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ZhteSvCxhM2R9z_YivkoD42UBrE-tvbGXkY1Pj_0yHapNBNKEnjf6udGevAgKtfKhXri9GnayehUbNSQyUT2XtqqDTmVbFFIrOvm_HJiRELhQ5mQZ6NMXLIfisxL2UaEVJyC2DXXjjaedOsobcSRhelnQ0QC3-wyVFXGX-XQCzbNcWRUhbTdCTG539kVDFFr6Dg-Htr5l-ZdDl-ly25QkOUdPwBt3hTVMa_vCkbqdqK3C7Ax7ygECFCbQ2rzYp1CmQ52AnaqSNHv5WdgSA' alt='Thermometers at the entrance of an Ebola treatment centre in Butembo, Democratic Republic of the Congo, in 2019.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Scale at declaration: Ars Technica reported that, although the outbreak was only then being publicized, it already ranked around the 10th-largest Ebola outbreak to date.</li><li>Response environment: Euronews reported that poverty and ethnic violence had weakened the health system, making protective measures difficult to organize.</li><li>Disease profile: Adom Online’s background noted that Ebola has no cure.</li><li>Symptoms: Early symptoms can include fever, muscle pain, fatigue, headache and sore throat.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Africa CDC: The agency said it was concerned about further spread because the outbreak risk extended to urban settings, not only remote communities. (<a href='https://www.sabcnews.com/sabcnews/ebola-outbreak-confirmed-in-drcs-ituri-province/'>SABC News</a>)</li><li>Health experts: The New York Times reported that experts were alarmed the outbreak had not been announced earlier, given the number of suspected infections and deaths already reported. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/15/world/africa/congo-ebola-outbreak.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Jean-Jacques Muyembe: The Congolese virologist told Reuters that a non-Zaire strain would complicate the response because existing countermeasures were designed for the Zaire strain. (<a href='https://www.annahar.com/international/world/310323/مراكز-مكافحة-الأمراض-الأفريقية-تعلن-تفشي-إيبولا-في-الكونغو-مع-65-وفاة'>An-Nahar</a>)</li><li>Ugandan authorities: Reports citing Ugandan officials said a 59-year-old man died Thursday in Kampala, and that officials characterized the case as imported rather than locally acquired. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-outbreak-confirmed-in-dr-congo-uganda-african-health-agency/a-77166606'>DW</a>, <a href='https://jyllands-posten.dk/international/ECE19301592/dr-congo-og-uganda-melder-om-udbrud-med-ebola/'>Jyllands-Posten</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3353735/africa-confirms-fatal-ebola-outbreak-congo-urgent-cross-border-meeting-called'>Africa confirms fatal Ebola outbreak in Congo, urgent cross-border meeting called</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/health/what-to-know-about-new-ebola-outbreak-that-has-killed-65-people-in-congo'>What to know about new Ebola outbreak that has killed 65 people in Congo</a>